@startuml
title Shadow - AI Change Set Lifecycle (ADR-015)

hide empty description

[*] --> draft : create_change_set (MCP, write grant)
draft --> draft : add_operations / remove_operation\n(scenario reference recomputed)\nvalidate_change_set (dry-run, always rolled back)
draft --> submitted : submit_change_set (creator's grant):\nre-validate, freeze generated values
draft --> discarded : discard_change_set (creator's grant)
submitted --> applied : human apply in Shadow (web), or\napply_change_set approved in the MCP client (mcp):\nlock, status, fingerprint, re-validate,\nexecute, commit once
submitted --> rejected : human reject in Shadow (web), or\nreject_change_set approved in the MCP client (mcp)
submitted --> failed : re-validation, operation or commit failure,\nor a lock or statement timeout during\nre-validation or execution
submitted --> submitted : apply rejected in the lock, status or\nfingerprint step (review_stale,\napply_in_progress, retryable 503)

note left of draft
  Only the creator's grants edit a draft.
  Dry-run stops at the first failing
  operation: ok, error, then not_run.
end note

note left of submitted
  Immutable. Only a human decides: in Shadow,
  or by approving apply_change_set or
  reject_change_set (MCP_CHANGE_SET_REVIEW_ENABLED).
  Replacement flags and the review fingerprint
  are recomputed against current data.
  The review records its channel (web or mcp).
end note

note bottom of applied
  Business rows written only through the
  domains' *_in_transaction cores; the
  reviewer is their actor.
end note

note bottom of failed
  Everything rolled back, then marked failed
  in a new transaction only while still
  submitted. Not retried; stage a new one.
end note

note bottom of rejected
  applied, rejected, failed and
  discarded are terminal.
end note

@enduml
